## Findings — worst first

### 1. East service alley, rect `[1059.5, 76.8, 1118.7, 361.3]` pt — 156.7 m² of blank back-corridor ships as customer floor, and `walk_truth` asserts it
**Evidence:** overlay crop pt 1030–1200 × 60–400; PDF crops of both wall gaps.
- Zero fixtures (29 cells of stray artwork), zero of the page's 265 printed words, 5.78 m × 27.8 m, **dead-ends against the north exterior wall**.
- Bounded east by the thick-walled H-E-B Curbside staging block `[1118.7,76.8,1181.6,361.3]`, west by the 12-pt wall band `[1047.3,131.5,1059.5,195.4]`/`[1047.6,209.3,1059.6,348.5]` whose east face (x=1059.5) is collinear with the Dairy back-of-house block's east face (x=1059.0).
- Only two openings, both ≈14 pt (1.36 m): y 195.4–209.3 and y 348.5–362.4.

This is the exact signature the repo treats as back-of-house elsewhere: store 388's exclusion `[979,58,1131,497]` seals "the empty receiving hall along the east wall x=1064-1128" on identical evidence, and 269's own NW-block exclusion is worded the same way.

**Why I did not apply it:** the guide draws no hatching, no door leaves and no staff marking here — unlike the north-band doorway at x=514.6–536.3, which has a double swing door drawn just inside it. And 269's front action alley is also ~190 m² of blank floor, so "blank" alone is not proof. Sealing 156.7 m² on inference is the error class this audit exists to prevent, so it needs a human eye.

**Truth should be:** staff back corridor, purple/untinted. **Fix:** exclusion `{"rect":[1059.5,76,1118.7,362]}` + `must_not [1090,250]`, and delete the current `must [1090,250,"east action alley…"]`, which asserts the opposite. Blocker on human confirmation.

